Here is the standard pattern:

### 1. The Idiomatic Approach (Variadic Parameters)

You define the parameter as a slice of the type (`[]string`) with the `...` operator. Inside the function, you check the length of the slice. If it's empty, you use the default value.

```go
package main

import "fmt"

// Define a variadic parameter
func greet(names ...string) {
    // If no arguments were passed, names is an empty slice
    if len(names) == 0 {
        names = []string{"Guest"} // Apply default value
    }

    for _, name := range names {
        fmt.Printf("Hello, %s!\n", name)
    }
}

func main() {
    // Call with no arguments -> uses default
    greet() 

    // Call with one argument
    greet("Alice")

    // Call with multiple arguments
    greet("Bob", "Charlie")
}
